I will make a quick comment on auto3Dgm . Looks like you have cut the meshes in half, which I assume for the speed of calculation in auto3Dgm. I can't see the surface of the cut plane from your screenshots, but in some software such operation this result in a completely flat surface. If you run meshes like that in auto3Dgm, your will end up with quite a bit of pseudoLMs points on that surface, which has no real morphological information. If that's the case, you may want to be mindful about what those points are contributing to your analysis.

