Regarding your comment about the nested approach. Are the following codes correct to assess differences between species, nested into clades? Or the correct order should be species/clade ?

fit_unique <- procD.lm(coords ~ log(Csize)*clade/species, SS.type = "III",

                                data = gdf, print.progress = FALSE)

fit_common <- procD.lm(coords ~ log(Csize) + clade/species, SS.type = "III",

                                data = gdf, print.progress = FALSE)

anova (fit_common, fit_unique)

Best. Thanks in advance

